(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "adr-2809051130-kototama-runtime-naming-unification")
  (:adr/title "KIR :runtime naming unification: kotoba-* to kototama-* host keywords (T0 contract)")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-05")
  (:adr/related (vector "ADR-2607102200" "ADR-2607279200"))
  (:adr/context
  "kotoba-kir src/kotoba/kir/target.cljc mixes two naming planes in the :runtime keyword of :kotoba.target-profile/v1: 20 profiles carried :kotoba-* keywords (:kotoba-supervisor-v1, :kotoba-cljs-host-v1, :kotoba-evm-host-v1, :kotoba-component-runtime-v2, per-OS supervisor variants, :kotoba-capability-host-v1 family) while 3 already carried :kototama-* (:kototama-js-host-v1, :kototama-worker-host-v1, :kototama-component-host-v1). The :runtime slot names the VM contract, and kototama is the VM contract repo (spec/kototama-vm-v1.edn) - a :kotoba-* runtime keyword silently claims that the kotoba-language plane, not the kototama contract, owns admission/linking/composition. Surveyed by the kototama consistency loop (cron 2026-09-05 09:55, ledger seq 1).")
  (:adr/decision
  "1. All :runtime keywords in target.cljc are unified to :kototama-* host naming. Rename table (each purely a keyword identity change, no behavior change): :kotoba-capability-host-v1 to :kototama-capability-host-v1; :kotoba-browser-host-v1 to :kototama-browser-host-v1; :kotoba-wasi-host-v1 to :kototama-wasi-host-v1; :kotoba-supervisor-v1 to :kototama-supervisor-v1; :kotoba-linux/macos/windows-supervisor-v1 to :kototama-linux/macos/windows-supervisor-v1 (x86_64 and aarch64 each); :kotoba-aiueos-user-v1 to :kototama-aiueos-user-v1; :kotoba-android-isolated-host-v1 to :kototama-android-isolated-host-v1; :kotoba-ios-static-host-v1 to :kototama-ios-static-host-v1; :kotoba-cljs-node/browser-host-v1 to :kototama-cljs-node/browser-host-v1; :kotoba-evm-host-v1 to :kototama-evm-host-v1; :kotoba-component-runtime-v2 to :kototama-component-runtime-v2. The 2 :runtime :none profiles (aiueos uefi/kernel) are unchanged. 2. The known consumer in kotoba-wasm (src/kotoba/wasm/core.cljc wasm-runtime target-to-host map and the :kotoba-capability-host/v1 compatibility-section constant) changes in the same change set: kotoba-kir 725cf212919864bc6049c1d185c4da8ac564daa3 + kotoba-wasm 92cabb14e5b950b3133375e7c41913dc773aba95. 3. Generated *.mjs.manifest.edn artifacts embed :runtime - they are regenerated by their generators, never hand-edited. amu fixture shas (test/kotoba/compiler/*_test.clj, test/fixtures/ios-aot-artifact.edn, scripts/android-ndk-conformance.cljs and windows-profile-conformance.cljs) migrate in the amu repo after the kir pin advances there.")
  (:adr/consequences
  "Verified: kotoba-kir test suite on the renamed tree - Ran 330 tests, 2221 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors (clojure -M:test, worktree loop/kototama-consistency-1). kotoba-wasm test suite on its renamed tree - Ran 131 tests, 548 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors. Consumers outside these two repos (kototama-native executor.clj, amu fixtures/tests) are recorded in the loop ledger as follow-up when their kir pin advances; they compile against the old keywords until then and are not silently broken because their pins still select the pre-rename kir commit. New profiles must use :kototama-* naming from now on.")))
